    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d121">

                <pb facs="0278" n="166" xml:id="pg166"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13079: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-11T11:00:00+08:00">May 11, 1935—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 11—2:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>192. Reference Legation’s 186, May 7, 10 a.m.<anchor n="42" xml:id="d121-f1"/>
                        Ringwalt<anchor n="43" xml:id="d121-f2"/> reports that Chiang Kai-shek
                    arrived at Yunnanfu on May 10th. He also reports that several thousand Reds are
                    believed to be still in the mountains north of Wuting and that the majority have
                    crossed the Yangtze River at various places above and below Tungan.</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
